  <name>QTerminator</name>
  <summary>Qt terminal emulator with splits, tabs, and plugin system</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      QTerminator is a Qt port of the Terminator terminal emulator,
      built with PyQt6 and QTermWidget. It allows arranging multiple
      terminal panes in tabs and recursive splits within one window.
    </p>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Tabs and recursive horizontal/vertical splits</li>
      <li>Per-terminal title bars with grouping indicators</li>
      <li>Broadcast input to grouped or all terminals</li>
      <li>Read-only mode, zoom, fullscreen, dark theme</li>
      <li>Configurable profiles and color schemes</li>
      <li>Layout save and restore across restarts</li>
      <li>Extensible Python plugin system with 19+ built-in plugins</li>
      <li>Terminator-compatible CLI options</li>
      <li>System dark/light theme detection</li>
      <li>URL detection and clickable issue tracker links</li>
      <li>Vim-like modal keybindings</li>
      <li>Tmux integration for persistent sessions</li>
      <li>Export buffer to HTML, PDF, or print</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
